Chapter: ConvolutionIdentity
  cites Signal chapter Convolution

 The box-3 line is deliberately NOT an identity and is here to pin a
 known imprecision rather than to bless it. kernel-box-3 is 333 333
 333, which sums to 999, so a smoothing filter that should have unity
 gain attenuates a constant by a part in a thousand on every pass.
 One third is not representable at scale 1000 and making the kernel
 334 333 333 would buy exactness for a constant at the cost of a
 lopsided kernel, so the number is recorded here and the choice is
 left where it is.

Section: Signals

  sig : List Integer
  sig = [100, 200, 300, 400, 500]

  impulse : List Integer
  impulse = [0, 1000, 0]

  flat : List Integer
  flat = [1000, 1000, 1000, 1000, 1000]

  conv-imp : List Integer
  conv-imp = convolve sig impulse

  conv-box : List Integer
  conv-box = convolve flat kernel-box-3

  five : List Integer -> Text
  five (xs) = show (list-at xs 0) & " " & show (list-at xs 1) & " " & show (list-at xs 2) & " " & show (list-at xs 3) & " " & show (list-at xs 4)

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("impulse-identity=" & five conv-imp)
    print-line-uni ("box3-on-constant=" & five conv-box)
    print-line-uni ("lengths=" & show (list-length conv-imp) & " " & show (list-length conv-box))
  end

